From 772ad06b171ed4f5a03299ea08c93ff91270d5a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sriman Cherukuru <srimancherukuru@Sriman-macbook.local>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:33:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sim,arch-x86: make the SE-mode page size a Process
 parameter (large-page emulation)

Add Process.page_size (default 4KiB).  The x86-64 process model builds its
EmulationPageTable with that page size, keeps brk/stack/mmap/vsyscall
boundaries aligned to it, reports it through AT_PAGESZ, and the x86 TLB
installs one entry per emulated page (logBytes from the page table) with a
trie key of page-number width in SE mode as well as FS mode.  Physical
memory is still allocated from the 4 KiB page pool; Process::allocateMem
takes a large page of slack and aligns the physical start so that a TLB
entry can cover a whole large page.  mmap() now treats an unaligned start
address without MAP_FIXED as the hint Linux says it is instead of failing
(musl's allocator hints at 4 KiB-aligned addresses).  Lets SE-mode
experiments compare 4 KiB, 64 KiB, 2 MiB ... pages without a full-system
kernel.

Assignment 3 (memory hierarchy), Sriman Cherukuru, Sep 2026.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
